title: 'pallet-multi-asset-bounties: keep an approved bounty when its funding payment fails'
doc:
  - audience: Runtime User
    description: |
      `fund_bounty` no longer reverts when the funding payment cannot be initiated, for example
      when the treasury does not hold enough of the asset at enactment. The bounty is stored in
      `FundingAttempted` with a `Failed` payment and `BountyFundingFailed` is emitted, so anyone
      can call `retry_payment` once the treasury can pay. `RejectOrigin` can close such a bounty
      with `close_bounty`; it is removed without a refund.
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      New event variant `BountyFundingFailed { index }`, appended to `Event`. No storage or call
      signature changes and no storage migration.
crates:
  - name: pallet-multi-asset-bounties
    bump: major
